From b0ad603b60998172298fee2cff5ca08bba84181c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 07:24:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06943/11362] [outer-loop] fix dict-candidate CNN discard bug;
 matched-budget A/B shows no capability delta

Backports the dict-normalization fix (_as_action_like) the perception-
grounding audit (docs/research-notes/arc-perception-grounding-audit-
2026-07-13.md) found missing from the shipped path.
FrameChangeScorer.candidate_score's getattr(candidate, "action_id") raised
AttributeError on dict-shaped candidates, silently discarding the CNN term
of the live default frame-change scorer -- a fix already existed for this
exact bug in arc_online_action_effect_scorer.py (a research-only scorer
variant), but was never backported to the shipped
arc_frame_change_predictor.py classes. Confirmed via the audit that this
fires on the live DEFAULT path (not just an optional/disabled feature) via
ActionEffectExpansionPrior.frontier_priority
(SUBMITTED_ACTION_EFFECT_EXPANSION_PRIOR_ENABLED=True, no other gate),
which is fed node["untested"] -- dict rows.

Fixed at the shared root (FrameChangeScorer.candidate_score itself, via a
new _as_action_like normalizer) rather than at call sites, so every
consumer benefits without call-site changes. Pure additive fix: verified
dict-shaped and object-shaped candidates now score identically, confirmed
the pre-fix code genuinely raised AttributeError (not a no-op change), and
the full 117-test regression sweep across every test file touching this
module passes clean.

Per CLAUDE.md's Phase Prototype + Empirical Validation + Adversarial Check
Discipline, a fix that stops a silent bug is not automatically a capability
win -- measured it with a matched-budget A/B (exp5590) across the full
11-game CLAIMED roster, CONTROL reproducing the pre-fix behavior via a
scoped _as_action_like identity monkeypatch, TREATMENT using the real fixed
default, tier-3 induction disabled to isolate the search/frontier-priority
effect. Result: levels_gained_headroom_present=true (1 level reached in
both arms, interpretable per FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK discipline), but
per_game_levels_delta is zero on every single game, and states_expanded
(distinct explored-state count) matched EXACTLY between arms for all 11
games -- a stronger null than "levels didn't change": the fix produced
literally zero measurable difference in explorer search behavior. Consistent
with the CNN term's already-small blend weight (cnn_weight=0.05 vs
memory_weight=1.0) and the project's prior LOO=chance finding on frame-only
features -- the underlying signal was not load-bearing at this weight,
not that the bug was inert. The fix remains correct code hygiene regardless.

First A/B run tripped adversarial_verify.py's TAUTOLOGY check on a
self-inflicted redundant combined_wall_clock_s field that structurally
always equaled duration_s in this script (no step separates the two timers,
unlike the sibling script this was modeled on); removed the redundant field
and re-ran rather than disclosing a coincidence that carried no information.
Re-run confirms the identical result; adversarial_verify.py and the ARC
artifact lint both now clean.

7 new tests (blocked-precondition fail-closed path, three synthetic outcome
classes -- positive delta, honest null with headroom, regression --, a
regression guard against the tautology field reappearing, and the
checked-in real-run artifact).

